{quote}So my question is, does {{   "scraped_time_slot": [}} mean the exact time of the trip? Can we drop it? If not, can we indicate the trip time by taking a longer period of time, e.g. by the hour?{quote}

It’s not exact time, but a 10-min interval when the trip happened. Unfortunately, we cannot drop it, because this field signifies when a similar route needs to be scraped. We can potentially do it by the hour, but this will introduce some bias to the data we collect vs the actual state of the marketplace. As an alternative, would introducing ±10 min noise work?


{quote}{{     "route_type": "airport",}} → What does this mean? I presume this example indicates that the trip was made to the airport. What would the route type be if the trip destination was something other than airport? Do we need this?{quote}

It’s a trip _from_ an airport. All other trips will have this field as {{non_airport}} – these are the only two options for this field. It’s necessary for this project, but also realistically even if we drop it, the pickup coordinates will tell whether it’s from an airport or not even with noise.

*One additional thing:* Anakin’s storage is located in Asia, so we’re transferring this data outside of the EU. Is it fine?

